SECURITY NOTES
==============

v2.0-safe includes:
  ✅ Input validation (IPv4, IPv6, ports)
  ✅ Pre-flight checks (port availability, SSH conflicts)
  ✅ Error handling (all critical operations)
  ✅ Isolated rule chains (no cross-service interference)
  ✅ Safe deletion (only own components)
  ✅ Safe restore (only own rules)
  ✅ Automatic backups (timestamped, incremental)
  ✅ 3-level SSH protection (no accidental blocking)

Known Limitations:
  • IPv6 MASQUERADE not implemented (socat is used instead)
  • Rules persist across reboots (stored by netfilter-persistent)
  • Only one instance of socat per port (systemd singleton)
  • Lock-port-to-IP requires knowledge of target IP and port

